<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_headinghuk5r4i8s7qe9" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 15 — Paragraph Between Numbered List in a Workflow</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a workflow where the author has inserted a &lt;p&gt; element between two numbered items</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Workflow</keyword>
        <keyword>workflow</keyword>
        <keyword>draft</keyword>
        <keyword>Paragraph</keyword>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <indexterm>Workflow</indexterm>
        <indexterm>workflow</indexterm>
        <indexterm>draft</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider a workflow where the author has inserted a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element between two numbered items to add explanatory text before continuing the numbered list.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Paragraph between stages in workflow</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;h2 id="approval-workflow">Approval Workflow&lt;/h2>
&lt;ol>
  &lt;li>
    Author submits the draft.
    &lt;p>Submissions are queued and reviewed in the order received.&lt;/p>
  &lt;/li>
  &lt;li>Reviewer approves or rejects the draft.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;concept id="approval_workflow">
  &lt;title>Approval Workflow&lt;/title>
  &lt;conbody>
    &lt;ol>
      &lt;li>
        Author submits the draft.
        &lt;p>Submissions are queued and reviewed in the order received.&lt;/p>
      &lt;/li>
      &lt;li>
        Reviewer approves or rejects the draft.
      &lt;/li>
    &lt;/ol>
  &lt;/conbody>
&lt;/concept></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element is nested inside the preceding <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> as a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element and does not split the <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;</codeph> into two independent lists.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
